 ### Local mode
 
-`IntervalTrainer.train_using_predictor(co2_predictor, interval_generator)` runs the same forecast and scheduling loop on your own machine. The training process runs in the local machine's process, and the trainer pauses during intervals outside the selected windows.
+`IntervalTrainer.train_using_predictor(co2_predictor, interval_generator)` forecasts, generates intervals, and trains during those intervals on your own machine. It re-generates intervals after the trainer has moved through the current list or once `minimum_prediction_period` seconds (default 3600) have passed. When the schedule is exhausted or empty, it stops and prints the emissions summary.
 
